---
title: 'Art — Faye Wai'
description: 'Paintings, pottery and illustration by Faye Wai — intuitive, abstract, layered work made in Port Moody, British Columbia. Commissions open.'
ogTitle: 'Art — Faye Wai'
ogDescription: 'Paintings, pottery and illustration by Faye Wai.'
ogImage: 'assets/social/art.jpg'
ogImageAlt: 'Three paintings by Faye Wai, captioned Art — painting, pottery, illustration'
---
{% from "work.njk" import tile %}
<main id="main">
<div class="wrap">

  <header class="hero hero--page">
    <div class="eyebrow-rule" style="margin-bottom:clamp(26px,4vh,44px)"><span class="eyebrow">Visual art</span></div>
    <h1 class="display h1--page">I paint to pay attention and stay with a feeling a little longer</h1>
    <div class="hero__intro hero__intro--media">
      <div class="frame frame--round r32"><img src="assets/faye-painting.jpg" alt="Faye at an easel in a studio, palette in one hand, brush to the canvas" fetchpriority="high"></div>
      <div>
      <p class="lede">Painting asks me to slow down, to work brush by brush. It requires me to respond to what is happening on the canvas, and let the image develop through a conversation rather than a fixed plan.</p>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>I’m interested in that moment when something begins to shift: when a colour changes the balance of a piece, when an unexpected mark opens a new direction. The best surprise is when I realise the painting is asking for something different than I intended.</p>
        <p>Painting, for me, is a practice of noticing, responding, and knowing when to keep going — as well as knowing when to stop.</p>
        <p><strong>The painting changes as I do.</strong></p>
      </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  {#- The series shown above the gallery. Everything it needs is in _data/series.js. -#}
  <section class="section--rule" style="padding:clamp(40px,6vh,70px) 0 clamp(60px,9vh,110px)" aria-labelledby="series-h">
    <div class="section-head section-head--stack" data-reveal>
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow" id="series-h">Selected works</span>
        <h2 class="h2" style="margin-top:14px">{{ series.title }}</h2>
        <p class="section-head__sub">{{ series.meta }}</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="tiles tiles--5" data-lightbox>
      {%- for w in series.works %}
      {{ tile(w, true, '', 'sq') }}
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>

  {#- The landscape paintings. Edit the list in _data/landscapes.js. -#}
  <section id="gallery" style="padding:0 0 clamp(60px,9vh,110px)" aria-labelledby="landscapes-h">
    <div class="section-head section-head--stack" data-reveal>
      <h2 class="h2" id="landscapes-h">Landscapes</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="tiles" data-lightbox style="margin-top:clamp(26px,4vh,44px)">
      {%- for w in landscapes %}
      {{ tile(w, true) }}
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>

  {#- Commissioned work, as a sideways rail. Edit the list in _data/commissions.js. -#}
  <section style="padding:0 0 clamp(60px,9vh,110px)" aria-labelledby="commissions-h" data-rail-group>
    <div class="section-head section-head--stack" data-reveal>
      <div>
        <h2 class="h2" id="commissions-h">Custom commissions</h2>
        <p class="section-head__sub">Made for a space</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rail__nav">
        <button type="button" data-rail-prev aria-label="Previous commissions">&#8592;</button>
        <button type="button" data-rail-next aria-label="Next commissions">&#8594;</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="rail" data-rail data-lightbox tabindex="0" role="group" aria-label="Commissioned work" style="margin-top:clamp(26px,4vh,44px)">
      {%- for w in commissions %}
      {{ tile(w, true) }}
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>

</div>


</main>
